This is a linux driver for the RTL9210 SSD reader developed by me for learning purposes. I used WSL2 on Ubuntu to develop and test the code. To connect the driver to your device, simply run the bash script (bind_rtl9210.sh) and you will see the status of the driver through the "rtl9210:" messages.

If you don't want to clutter your terminal with the giant diagnostic messages, feel free to modify or remove the dmesg line in the bash script.

Below is the hardware descriptor information. For the full length copy, check out descriptors.txt in /docs

Hardware
========

Device Descriptor
-----------------
* USB Type: 3.20
* Vendor:   0x0bda Realtek Semiconductor Corp.
* Product:  0x9210 RTL9210 M.2 NVME Adapter

Interface Descriptor
--------------------
* Interface Class:    Mass Storage
* Interface Subclass: SCSI
* Interface Protocol: Bulk-Only

Endpoint Descriptors (UAS Mode)
-------------------------------
* Data-in  (0x03) Endpoint Address: 0x81 EP 1 IN
* Data-out (0x04) Endpoint Address: 0x02 EP 2 OUT
* Status   (0x02) Endpoint Address: 0x83 EP 3 IN
* Command  (0x01) Endpoint Address: 0x04 EP 4 OUT
